    "result_text": "The full suite (BUILD SUCCESS) passes. The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a per-city owner cap that rejects owner creation with **409 Conflict** when the target city already contains 50 or more owners. Following the codebase's existing validator/exception/advice pattern (mirroring `HouseholdDuplicateValidator` / `DuplicateHouseholdException`):\n\n1. **`CityOwnerLimitExceededException`** (`rest/error/`) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the rejected city, parallel to the other domain exceptions.\n\n2. **`CityOwnerLimitValidator`** (`rest/validation/`) \u2014 a single-responsibility `@Component` that reuses the existing `ClinicService.countOwnersInCity(...)` method and throws when the count is `>= 50` (constant `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY`).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 injected the new validator and invoked `cityOwnerLimitValidator.validate(...)` alongside the other request validators, keeping the controller thin.\n\n4. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added a handler mapping the new exception to a 409 `ProblemDetail` naming the `city` field, consistent with the existing duplicate-conflict handlers.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st to be rejected) passes, and the full suite reports **BUILD SUCCESS** with no failures.",
